    {
        "id": "what-does-footnote-do-differently",
        "question": "What does Footnote do differently from other AI tools?",
        "response": {
            "action": "message",
            "message": "Footnote is designed to be more transparent and decision-support oriented than many AI tools.\n\nKey differences:\n\n- **Provenance first**: it emphasizes where claims come from, so you can trace reasoning instead of treating output as a black box.\n- **Human oversight**: it’s built to support your judgment, not replace it.\n- **Clear trade-offs**: it helps compare options and values, rather than only optimizing for a single “best” answer.\n- **Interpretability over flair**: it aims for plain, accountable explanations instead of polished but opaque responses.\n- **Open-source orientation**: it’s part of an open project, which usually means more visibility into how it works and how it can be audited.\n\nIn short: many AI tools try to be fast or impressive; Footnote tries to be **clear, accountable, and easy to reason about**.",
            "modality": "text",
